# DEL-04-01 VER-007, the dense finish's constructed system: a dense solve that does not meet
# REQ-014's limit within the kernel's refinement policy (no ordering is involved).
# Binary64 values as f64::to_bits in hex: the line "n N", then the N rows of K, then "f ..."
# (the load) and "x ..." (the solution the load was built from).
#
# Construction (core/solver/frame_kernel/tests/residual_refusal_witnesses.rs regenerates it and
# asserts every bit; no product code is needed given t's bits):
#   splitmix64, state s: s += 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15; z = s; z = (z ^ (z >> 30)) * 0xBF58476D1CE4E5B9;
#     z = (z ^ (z >> 27)) * 0x94D049BB133111EB; next = z ^ (z >> 31)   (wrapping 64-bit)
#   Arrowhead, n = 96: hub DOF 0 joined to leaf j = 1..95 by a spring 2^(next % 31); then each
#     leaf grounded by (1 + next % 7) / t; the hub grounded by 1 / t. Generator seeded
#     11000 + 977*8 + 96. K[0][0] = 1/t, then += each spring in leaf order;
#     K[j][j] = spring_j + ground_j; K[0][j] = K[j][0] = -spring_j; every other entry 0.
#   t = f64::from_bits(0x411a63a067f6457d), about 2^18.721874. It was placed by bisecting the ground knob to
#     the kernel's condition-gate boundary for this structure (2^22.218640286, admitted below it) and
#     stepping down 10/19 of two decades. Only this placement used kernel code.
#   x: generator seeded 12000 + 8 + 7*10 + 46; x[i] = 2^46 for odd i (the leaves
#     1, 3, ...), else 2^(next % 4); each times a sign (next % 2 == 0 -> +1, else -1); drawn per
#     entry in that order, the exponent draw skipped for the 2^46 entries.
#   f[i] = sum over j of K[i][j] * x[j], left to right in binary64.
#
# What it shows, and what it does not:
#   - dense finish: no result and the named finding "original-equation residual failed after
#     bounded refinement". The refinement stopped on non-improvement (worst row 2.16 of the limit
#     at the first solve, 2.90 after one correction), not on exhausted attempts; read from an
#     instrumented scratch build, as the kernel does not expose which.
#   - the same system in the sparse finish returns a result marked sensitive meeting REQ-014 row
#     by row: under the product's ordering (sparse_direct's reverse Cuthill-McKee, both entries)
#     at the first solve, and under natural order after one refinement. This solve does not meet
#     the limit within the kernel's refinement policy; the system is not one that cannot.
n 96
